From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laine Walker-Avina <lwalkera@ieee.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:11:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Beken: enable DST rules (time_setDST)

The SSS10's MCU runs its schedules on the local time it gets from the
Wi-Fi module, so the clock must follow daylight saving time. The DST
code already exists for other platforms; turn it on for Beken.

Example (most of the US: second Sunday of March 2:00 to first Sunday of
November 2:00, 60 minutes):

    time_setDST 2 3 1 2 60 1 11 1 2 0
---
 src/obk_config.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/obk_config.h b/src/obk_config.h
index 2d943abc..16babc07 100644
--- a/src/obk_config.h
+++ b/src/obk_config.h
@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@
 #define ENABLE_TASMOTADEVICEGROUPS				1
 #define ENABLE_LITTLEFS							1
 #define ENABLE_NTP								1
-// #define ENABLE_TIME_DST						1
+#define ENABLE_TIME_DST							1
 #define ENABLE_TIME_SUNRISE_SUNSET				1
 #define ENABLE_DRIVER_LED						1
 #define ENABLE_DRIVER_BL0937					1
